# Cloudflare Pages headers (https://developers.cloudflare.com/pages/configuration/headers/).
# The PWA comes from vite-plugin-pwa (Workbox): the service worker precaches by content hash and updates itself. At the
# EDGE, what matters:
#  • sw.js / index.html / manifest ALWAYS fresh → the PWA's update mechanism works (no "stale build stuck"). This build
#    emits no `index.html` since the cartridge left (#111); its rule is harmless without one.
#  • Vite's hashed bundles (/assets/*-[hash].*) are safely immutable (the name changes when the content changes).
# Caveat: /assets/* also catches any NON-hashed static of public/assets/. Such files change rarely and the service
# worker covers the offline client; if one changes without a new hash, purge the CF cache (or separate Vite's
# build.assetsDir). There are no /js/* or /css/* rules: Vite bundles into /assets/. The fonts under /vendor/ have
# their own rules at the end of this file.

# CONTENT-SECURITY-POLICY (issue #170; narrowed by ADR-0177, issue #173): which hosts may run script and be fetched.
#  • script-src: this origin; `'wasm-unsafe-eval'` — the
#    voice and vision runtimes compile WebAssembly. No third-party host: the game bundles its runtimes.
#  • connect-src: this origin only. The heavy files come from the delivery's own `heavy/` (ADR-0177), so the catalogue's
#    hosts are contacted by the build alone; no library left in the engine requests a third party by itself (ADR-0207).
#  • style-src 'unsafe-inline': eight panel modules write `style="…"` through innerHTML (measured 2026-09-13).
# CROSS-ORIGIN ISOLATION (ADR-0192, issue #186): onnxruntime's WASM runs the voices on threads only in an isolated page — a 3 s
#  Kokoro sentence took 8.7 s on one thread and 2.7 s on threads (measured). The price: a subresource from another origin loads
#  only by CORS or CORP, so the delivery carries its own. No narrower rule below may send or detach either header.
/*
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
  Cross-Origin-Embedder-Policy: require-corp
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self' 'wasm-unsafe-eval'; worker-src 'self' blob:; connect-src 'self'; style-src 'self' 'unsafe-inline'; img-src 'self' data: blob:; font-src 'self' data:; media-src 'self' blob:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'self'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'self'

/sw.js
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/index.html
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/manifest.webmanifest
  Cache-Control: no-cache
/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
# 🔴 THE FONTS ARE IMMUTABLE; THE INDEX OF THEM IS NOT. `vendor/fonts.css` declares all 166 families and its NAME NEVER CHANGES,
# so a year of `immutable` freezes the list itself: a browser that read it once offers last term's faces, and a family added
# later is chosen in the menu and drawn by the system font, with nothing failing anywhere. It is the frozen-precache defect of
# `scripts/check-precache.mjs` one layer up, at the edge.
#  📏 Measured 2026-09-21: the SERVICE WORKER is not exposed — Workbox fetches a revisioned entry under `?__WB_REVISION__=…`
#  (present in the built `workbox-*.js`), a URL the immutable rule never matched. What is exposed is every client without one:
#  a private window, a browser where the worker never installs, the first load before it does, and a consumer page that links
#  this stylesheet and registers no worker.
#  📌 TWO PATTERNS THAT DO NOT OVERLAP, on purpose: a single `/vendor/*` plus a narrower rule would depend on which of them
#  Cloudflare applies first, which is not written here and cannot be measured from this repository. The 346 woff2 live under
#  `/vendor/fonts/` and keep the year; the index revalidates, which costs a 304 and never a stale menu.
/vendor/fonts/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
/vendor/fonts.css
  Cache-Control: public, no-cache
# The fonts' NOTICE and licence texts (scripts/licences/fonts.mjs) live BESIDE `fonts/`, not in it, for the same reason as the
# index: the notice changes whenever a family does, and a year of `immutable` would keep last term's list on a browser with no
# service worker. A third pattern that overlaps neither of the two above.
/vendor/fonts-licences/*
  Cache-Control: public, no-cache
